<header><p class="st-kicker">republic · Balkans and Hungary</p><h1 class="st-title">Hungarian Democratic Republic</h1><p class="st-meta">1918 CE – 1919 CE · capital Budapest</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Hungary's first republic, born of the Aster Revolution of 1918, which collapsed under the pressure of defeat and territorial losses.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>As <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austro-hungarian-empire">Austria-Hungary</a> collapsed at the end of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-world-war">First World War</a>, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aster-revolution">Aster Revolution</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/budapest">Budapest</a> on 31 October 1918 brought Count <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mihaly-karolyi">Mihály Károlyi</a> to power as prime minister; on the same day former premier <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/istvan-tisza">István Tisza</a> was murdered. On 16 November 1918 the National Council proclaimed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hungary">Hungary</a> a republic, ending the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-hungary-1867-1918">Kingdom of Hungary</a> (1867-1918).</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mihaly-karolyi">Károlyi</a>'s coalition of liberals, radicals and Social Democrats introduced universal suffrage and began land reform, distributing his own estate. But it faced economic chaos, returning soldiers and the advance of Czechoslovak, Romanian and Serbian troops beyond the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/belgrade">Belgrade</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/armistice-of-11-november-1918">armistice</a> lines. Károlyi became provisional president in January 1919, with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/denes-berinkey">Dénes Berinkey</a> as prime minister.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>In March 1919 the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/allies">Allies</a>' <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vix-note">Vix Note</a> demanded a further Hungarian withdrawal in the east. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mihaly-karolyi">Károlyi</a>'s government resigned, and the Social Democrats united with the Communists, who proclaimed the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/hungarian-soviet-republic">Hungarian Soviet Republic</a> on 21 March 1919.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/hungarian-democratic-republic.jpg" alt="Hungarian Democratic Republic" width="320" height="160"><figcaption>Image: Thommy · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Hungary_(1918%E2%80%931919).svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1918 CE – 1919 CE</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>republic</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>bureaucratic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Budapest</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Mihály Károlyi, Dénes Berinkey</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Catholic and Protestant Christianity</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Hungarian</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/hungary">Hungary</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>First Hungarian Republic, Hungarian People's Republic (1918)</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1918&amp;focus=hungarian-democratic-republic" aria-label="Hungarian Democratic Republic on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5125 512 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Hungarian Democratic Republic lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5445 768L5445 768M5445 768L5445 768"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5445 768h0M5445 768h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5445 768h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5445 768h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Budapest. <a href="/atlas?year=1918&amp;focus=hungarian-democratic-republic">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
